    {
      "text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored. If the backup fails during a crisis, it is not a backup\u2014it is an archive.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundational Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data redundancy:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your original data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media",
